# ============================== YEAR 6 ==============================
R(6, "Fat years, large families", "double1")
act("Graham turns the fifth I Ching card: Population Doubles. A good harvest for every province, and no disasters. The population doubles to 300 million, x3, and every province eats twice what it did. New land opens (Section 13): from now on any province may buy squares at 20 each, the Emperor paying part of every other province's square.", map_hl=[1,5,6,7])
say("Graham", "\"Population Doubles.\" It's a good harvest everywhere, and the counter goes from 150 million to 300 million. That's times three. Everyone moves down to the x3 row, and consumption doubles with it. No disasters this year. New land is open at twenty a square. Silke, the crown is allowed to pay part of it, so I suggest you think about who's going to pay your tax next year.",
 "Graham: This is the number I've been waiting for: a square at twenty that pays twenty a year. At x3 my average income is minus twenty-five, so I'll buy land before I spend a grain on anyone's pottery. The Jar can wait one more year.")
harvest("Graham pays out the harvest from the Harvest Pile; a negative income is paid into it.")
act("The Storyteller gives Silke a public tip: the crown may pay any part of a province's square, up to all of it; every square it helps buy raises that province's income, and so the tax it can pay; and her board card shows how many squares Province 1 needs to break even.", map_hl=[1])
say("Silke", "Nobody owes a grain this year, so I won't pretend to collect one. Ten percent on nothing is nothing. Reina, here's the coast canal I said was coming, the first section of it, paid for by the crown. And every one of you who breaks new ground this year gets half of each square from me. Buy land. A hungry province is no use to me or to you.",
 "Silke: The doubling just wiped out everyone's income, mine included, so I'm putting the reserve into the soil: two squares for my own province, half of every square for theirs, and a canal that makes Reina's harvest taxable again. I'm leaving the Great Wall alone for now. With a hundred and twenty I can't build both of the last works, and I'm not ending this game until I'm sure the treasury will hold.")
taxes(.10, collector="Paddy collects the tax for the crown: nobody's income is positive, so nobody owes any")
build("Grand Canal", 40, {1:40}, canal={5:1}, text="Public works: Silke digs the first section of the Grand Canal in Province 5, the year's one project. It adds 10 to Reina's harvest from next year.", hover="Silke pays the 40, into the Harvest Pile. 280 of the works are still owed: the four Wall links and three canal sections.")
buy_land(1, ["F23", "F24"], {1:40}, text="New land: Silke buys two squares of sea for Province 1, F23 and F24, for 40 from the crown's reserve. Each adds 20 to her harvest from next year.", hover="The crown also offers to pay half, 10, of every square another province buys this year.")
act("The Storyteller gives each peasant the same public tip before they answer: a square bought this year starts yielding with next year's harvest and pays for itself in a year; their board card shows how many they need to break even, now and after the next card; and a player in debt can't buy any.", map_hl=[5,6,7])
say("Reina", "Silke, that's a promise kept in front of everyone and I'll say so: the coast canal is dug. I'll take you up on the half, two squares on the coast, ten from me and ten from the crown on each. A fed Province 5 pays you tax next year instead of a revolt.",
 "Reina: Two squares is what my card says I need to break even, and at ten grain each I can just about afford them. It leaves me with five, so the throne waits a year. I'd rather climb back slowly than be the province that tips into debt with the end in sight.")
buy_land(5, ["O27", "P27"], {5:20, 1:20}, text="New land: Reina buys two squares of sea for Province 5, O27 and P27, 40 in all, half from Reina and half from the crown. Each adds 20 to her harvest from next year.")
say("Paddy", "Thank you, Silke, I'll take you at your word, same as Reina did: two squares of paddy on the coast, R25 and R26, ten from me and ten from the crown on each. Rice doesn't grow on promises, but it grows on new mud right enough.",
 "Paddy: Three squares would have fed us for certain, but the crown's only got twenty left to share and I won't spend the twenty I'm keeping back for the Vase. With two I'm only about five short in an average year, and I'm not in debt to anybody.")
buy_land(6, ["R25", "R26"], {6:20, 1:20}, text="New land: Paddy buys two squares of sea for Province 6, R25 and R26, 40 in all, half from Paddy and half from the crown. Each adds 20 to his harvest from next year.", hover="That empties the crown's reserve: it can pay no share of another square this year.")
say("Graham", "Silke, your purse is empty, but you owe me five for the reading, and the rules say the crown pays some part of every square. So pay one grain a square out of what you owe me and I'll pay the other nineteen. Three squares of wheat in Province 7, and you don't have to find a grain you haven't got.",
 "Graham: Three squares turns my minus twenty-five into plus thirty-five, and they pay for themselves even if the game ends next year. That leaves me about forty-six, enough for the twenty I'll need when Paddy is finally ready to talk about the Jar.")
say("Silke", "Graham, that's the most gracious way anyone has ever asked me for money I don't have. Done. One grain a square from your salary, three squares of wheat for Province 7, and I still owe you two at year's end. Write it down so nobody says the crown forgot.",
 "Silke: I spent the treasury down to nothing on purpose. Every square on the board this year is a province that can pay tax next year, and Graham just paid for most of his own share while letting me keep my word on the rules. Next year I need those harvests in, because I can't build the Wall on an empty purse, and until I can, nobody's ending this game.")
act("The crown has no grain to pay its share with, so Graham hands Silke 3 against this year's I Ching salary, and the crown pays it straight back as its 1 a square. By their deal the crown still owes Graham 2 for the year.", deltas={pid(7):-3, pid(1):3}, map_hl=[1,7], deal=True)
buy_land(7, ["T15", "T16", "T17"], {7:57, 1:3}, text="New land: Graham buys three squares of the Warlord's land for Province 7, T15, T16 and T17, 60 in all: 57 from Graham and 3 from the crown. Each adds 20 to his harvest from next year.", hover="Graham has paid 60 in all for the three squares, and has 43.5 left.")
